{title: Wonderful Peace}
{key: Ab}
{x_theme: prayer, name-of-jesus, praise}
{x_source: chrd:wonderful_peace.chrd}

{comment: Chorus}
[Ab]Peace, peace, [Db]wonderful [Ab]peace,
Coming [Fm]down from the [Bb7]Father a[Eb]bove!
Sweep [Ab]over my spirit for[Db]ever, I pray
In [Ab]fathomless bil[Eb7]lows of [Ab]love!

{comment: Verse 1}
Far a[Ab]way in the depths of my [Db]spirit [Ab]tonight
Rolls a melody [Bb7]sweeter than [Eb]psalm;
In ce[Ab]lestial-like strains it un[Db]ceasingly [Ab]falls
O'er my soul like an [Eb7]infinite [Ab]calm.

{comment: Verse 2}
What a [Ab]treasure I have in this [Db]wonderful [Ab]peace,
Buried deep in the [Bb7]heart of my [Eb]soul,
So [Ab]secure that no power can [Db]mine it a[Ab]way,
While the years of [Eb7]eternity [Ab]roll!

{comment: Verse 3}
I am [Ab]resting tonight in this [Db]wonderful [Ab]peace,
Resting sweetly in [Bb7]Jesus' con[Eb]trol;
For I'm [Ab]kept from all danger by [Db]night and by [Ab]day,
And His glory is [Eb7]flooding my [Ab]soul!

{comment: Verse 4}
And I [Ab]think when I rise to that [Db]city of [Ab]peace,
Where the Author of [Bb7]peace I shall [Eb]see,
That one [Ab]strain of the song which the [Db]ransomed will [Ab]sing
In that heavenly [Eb7]kingdom will [Ab]be!

{comment: Verse 5}
Ah [Ab]soul, are you here without [Db]comfort and [Ab]rest,
Marching down the rough [Bb7]pathway of [Eb]time?
Make [Ab]Jesus your friend ere the [Db]shadows grow [Ab]dark;
Oh, accept this sweet [Eb7]peace so sub[Ab]lime!
